                   Yang, Shulin and Legrand, Thomas",
  journal       = "arXiv [cs.IR]",
  abstract      = "One of the long-standing questions in search systems is the
                   role of diversity in results. From a product perspective,
                   showing diverse results provides the user with more choice
                   and should lead to an improved experience. However, this
                   intuition is at odds with common machine learning approaches
                   to ranking which directly optimize the relevance of each
                   individual item without a holistic view of the result set. In
