@ARTICLE{Duan2021-eb,
  title         = "Online experimentation with surrogate metrics: Guidelines and
                   a case study",
  author        = "Duan, Weitao and Ba, Shan and Zhang, Chunzhe",
  journal       = "arXiv [stat.AP]",
  abstract      = "A/B tests have been widely adopted across industries as the
                   golden rule that guides decision making. However, the
                   long-term true north metrics we ultimately want to drive
                   through A/B test may take a long time to mature. In these
                   situations, a surrogate metric which predicts the long-term
                   metric is often used instead to conclude whether the
                   treatment is effective. However, because the surrogate rarely
                   predicts the true north perfectly, a regular A/B test based
                   on surrogate metrics tends to have high false positive rate
                   and the treatment variant deemed favorable from the test may
                   not be the winning one. In this paper, we discuss how to
